# Gate step 1843-dex5 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. with-tillandsias-builder.sh decides whether to `toolbox
# create` from _toolbox_exists. When `toolbox list` failed once, it answered
# "absent" for a builder that had been up 43 h, ran create, and died "already
# exists" — evicting #612 from the land queue (macuahuitl 2026-10-23). The
# fixture extracts the function and drives it with stub toolbox/podman.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf); ported to Lua (2080-zcur).
STEP_DESC="Checking the builder does not mistake a failed toolbox list for an absent container (1843-dex5)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-builder-toolbox-exists.lua"
STEP_ERROR="with-tillandsias-builder.sh can again read a transient toolbox-list failure as an absent builder and try to recreate it (1843-dex5); see which arm failed above"
STEP_OK="builder existence check survives a failed toolbox list"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macuahuitl 2026-10-23 darwin skip:linux-only — toolbox and with-tillandsias-builder.sh are the Linux build path; darwin builds natively and never calls _toolbox_exists (1843-dex5)"
